    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
    "body": "While my primary themes are all mini.hues, I did spend yesterday (I'm on vacation this week) [tuning](https://github.com/pkazmier/nvim/commit/558c7c518925eb6d514f168d48e1a2a6a9827ec6) all four of sainnhe's colorschemes ([Everforest](https://github.com/sainnhe/everforest), [Gruvbox-Material](https://github.com/sainnhe/gruvbox-material), [Edge](https://github.com/sainnhe/edge), and [Sonokai](https://github.com/sainnhe/sonokai)) to my liking as secondaries themes. In doing so, I noticed a two mini highlight groups that need tweaking in all four themes. Specifically, `MiniPickPrompt` and `MiniFilesFile`. \r\n\r\nI was going to submit PRs to the projects for all four, but I thought it might be a good idea to confirm with you if you had any other tweaks you were planning that these could be queued up with so as to not overwhelm the maintainer. Obviously, I've already fixed these in my configurations, but wanted to make sure other mini users had a good experience out-of-the-box so to speak if they use those themes.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n`MiniPickPrompt` does not blend with the background of the float:\r\n<img width=\"1295\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/747855/0104f48e-7d1f-45da-851c-6f03a69b96d7\">\r\n\r\n`MiniFilesFile` does not look right if the cursor line is enabled:\r\n<img width=\"1295\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/747855/bc572339-6fab-4e3b-8578-c73049032522\">\r\n\r\nMy fixes for both:\r\n```lua\r\n    set_hl(\"MiniPickPrompt\", palette.blue,   config.float_style == \"dim\" and palette.bg_dim or palette.bg2)\r\n    set_hl(\"MiniFilesFile\",  palette.fg,     palette.none)\r\n```\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">While my primary themes are all mini.hues, I did spend yesterday (I'm on vacation this week) <a href=\"https://github.com/pkazmier/nvim/commit/558c7c518925eb6d514f168d48e1a2a6a9827ec6\">tuning</a> all four of sainnhe's colorschemes (<a href=\"https://github.com/sainnhe/everforest\">Everforest</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/sainnhe/gruvbox-material\">Gruvbox-Material</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/sainnhe/edge\">Edge</a>, and <a href=\"https://github.com/sainnhe/sonokai\">Sonokai</a>) to my liking as secondaries themes. In doing so, I noticed a two mini highlight groups that need tweaking in all four themes. Specifically, <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPickPrompt</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFilesFile</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I was going to submit PRs to the projects for all four, but I thought it might be a good idea to confirm with you if you had any other tweaks you were planning that these could be queued up with so as to not overwhelm the maintainer. Obviously, I've already fixed these in my configurations, but wanted to make sure other mini users had a good experience out-of-the-box so to speak if they use those themes.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPickPrompt</code> does not blend with the background of the float:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/747855/347410008-0104f48e-7d1f-45da-851c-6f03a69b96d7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTM0MjksIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzEyOSwicGF0aCI6Ii83NDc4NTUvMzQ3NDEwMDA4LTAxMDRmNDhlLTdkMWYtNDVkYS04NTFjLTZmMDNhNjliOTZkNy5wbmc_.aLtZX1t6Rnt0H4LySyaeZxPIBaSDcRjWamZ2X4mT70o\"><img width=\"1295\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/747855/347410008-0104f48e-7d1f-45da-851c-6f03a69b96d7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTM0MjksIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzEyOSwicGF0aCI6Ii83NDc4NTUvMzQ3NDEwMDA4LTAxMDRmNDhlLTdkMWYtNDVkYS04NTFjLTZmMDNhNjliOTZkNy5wbmc_.aLtZX1t6Rnt0H4LySyaeZxPIBaSDcRjWamZ2X4mT70o\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFilesFile</code> does not look right if the cursor line is enabled:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/747855/347410701-bc572339-6fab-4e3b-8578-c73049032522.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTM0MjksIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzEyOSwicGF0aCI6Ii83NDc4NTUvMzQ3NDEwNzAxLWJjNTcyMzM5LTZmYWItNGUzYi04NTc4LWM3MzA0OTAzMjUyMi5wbmc_.aIeAMmx_DTouUcRN8DBQcxlxw4-uRUIjqyvghlm6lDk\"><img width=\"1295\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/747855/347410701-bc572339-6fab-4e3b-8578-c73049032522.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTM0MjksIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzEyOSwicGF0aCI6Ii83NDc4NTUvMzQ3NDEwNzAxLWJjNTcyMzM5LTZmYWItNGUzYi04NTc4LWM3MzA0OTAzMjUyMi5wbmc_.aIeAMmx_DTouUcRN8DBQcxlxw4-uRUIjqyvghlm6lDk\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My fixes for both:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    set_hl(&quot;MiniPickPrompt&quot;, palette.blue,   config.float_style == &quot;dim&quot; and palette.bg_dim or palette.bg2)\n    set_hl(&quot;MiniFilesFile&quot;,  palette.fg,     palette.none)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">    <span class=\"pl-c1\">set_hl</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>MiniPickPrompt<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">palette</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">blue</span>,   <span class=\"pl-smi\">config</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">float_style</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>dim<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">palette</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bg_dim</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">palette</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bg2</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">set_hl</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>MiniFilesFile<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,  <span class=\"pl-smi\">palette</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fg</span>,     <span class=\"pl-smi\">palette</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">none</span>)</pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "While my primary themes are all mini.hues, I did spend yesterday (I'm on vacation this week) tuning all four of sainnhe's colorschemes (Everforest, Gruvbox-Material, Edge, and Sonokai) to my liking as secondaries themes. In doing so, I noticed a two mini highlight groups that need tweaking in all four themes. Specifically, MiniPickPrompt and MiniFilesFile.\nI was going to submit PRs to the projects for all four, but I thought it might be a good idea to confirm with you if you had any other tweaks you were planning that these could be queued up with so as to not overwhelm the maintainer. Obviously, I've already fixed these in my configurations, but wanted to make sure other mini users had a good experience out-of-the-box so to speak if they use those themes.\n\nMiniPickPrompt does not blend with the background of the float:\n\nMiniFilesFile does not look right if the cursor line is enabled:\n\nMy fixes for both:\n    set_hl(\"MiniPickPrompt\", palette.blue,   config.float_style == \"dim\" and palette.bg_dim or palette.bg2)\n    set_hl(\"MiniFilesFile\",  palette.fg,     palette.none)",
