            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yep, I agree with both of these changes.\r\n\r\nThe \"MiniPickPrompt\" I tried to match the style of \"FloatTitle\": if in color scheme it has the same background as \"NormalFloat\", then so should be a \"MiniPickPrompt\". This is the case at least in 'everforest', so makes sense to adjust \"MiniPickPrompt\".\r\n\r\nThe \"MiniFilesFile\" one I simply missed when playtesting before making PRs. Yes, ideally it should not define background.\r\n\r\n(I must have been starting to feel exhaustion at this point when making all those color scheme PRs :sweat_smile:)",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yep, I agree with both of these changes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The \"MiniPickPrompt\" I tried to match the style of \"FloatTitle\": if in color scheme it has the same background as \"NormalFloat\", then so should be a \"MiniPickPrompt\". This is the case at least in 'everforest', so makes sense to adjust \"MiniPickPrompt\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The \"MiniFilesFile\" one I simply missed when playtesting before making PRs. Yes, ideally it should not define background.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">(I must have been starting to feel exhaustion at this point when making all those color scheme PRs 😅)</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yep, I agree with both of these changes.\nThe \"MiniPickPrompt\" I tried to match the style of \"FloatTitle\": if in color scheme it has the same background as \"NormalFloat\", then so should be a \"MiniPickPrompt\". This is the case at least in 'everforest', so makes sense to adjust \"MiniPickPrompt\".\nThe \"MiniFilesFile\" one I simply missed when playtesting before making PRs. Yes, ideally it should not define background.\n(I must have been starting to feel exhaustion at this point when making all those color scheme PRs 😅)",
